A</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>GORAB MAJUMDAR</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAGAMI TOORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWASAKI MITSUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KHALID HASSAN HUSSEIN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>GORAB, MAJUMDAR</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAGAMI, TOORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWASAKI, MITSUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KHALID HASSAN, HUSSEIN</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An inverter circuit, more particularly, an inverter circuit for supplying polyphase power, in which the resistance for detecting an overcurrent is low and the number of filters is small. Transistors (20S, 21S, 22S) each having a current detection terminal and a diode for protection from a regenerative current are provided as "L"-side switching elements and the current detection terminals are connected in common to a resistor (30s). A voltage drop caused by a current flowing through the resistor (30s) becomes large when an overcurrent flows through even any one of the transistors (20S, 21S, 22S), and further, when an overcurrent flows through "H"-side switching elements even if no overcurrent flows through any of the transistors (20S, 21S, 22S).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un circuit onduleur, notamment un circuit onduleur servant à délivrer un courant polyphasé, et présentant une faible résistance de détection de surintensité pour un petit nombre de filtres. Les éléments de commutation côté bas (L) sont réalisés à base de transistors (20S, 21S, 22S) comportant chacun une borne de détection d'intensité, et d'une diode de protection contre le courant de régénération. Les bornes de détection d'intensité sont connectées à une résistance commune (30s). Le passage de courant dans la résistance (30s) provoque une chute de tension qui a tendance à devenir d'autant plus importante que l'un quelconque des transistors (20S, 21S, 22S) est traversé par une surintensité, et qu'en outre, les éléments de commutation côté haut (H) sont traversés par une surintensité, même en l'absence de surintensité traversant l'un quelconque des transistors (20S, 21S, 22S).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>